# Train 5: p5-lifecycle-osc-hostile in a session that claims truecolor (COLORTERM=truecolor, as the
# `-tc` twins on main): the frames osc.py reads, every grey as each product spells it
# under truecolor. Captured from a scratch copy of the scenario directory
# (FXCAP_SCENARIOS); not a scenario of the repository. The rest is the twin's:
# Phase 5 L-U1 security: a command whose label carries bidi overrides and a
# tab, and a question whose text carries ESC, BEL, an OSC, NEL, a CSI and a
# bidi override -- on the wire only as base64 in `msg`, folded to one line
# without a control character. Each product's own command tool.
env COLORTERM=truecolor
fx: gateway p5-lifecycle-osc-hostile-fx.json
xfx: gateway p5-lifecycle-osc-hostile-xfx.json
fx: seed p5-lifecycle-ask-settings.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
xfx: env XFX_SOUND=off
wait 4
type run the command
key Enter
wait 3
wire h00-permission
key 1
wait 3
type ask me
key Enter
wait 3
wire h01-question
key 1
wait 3
keep
type /quit
key Enter
wait 2
wire h02-exit
